--- (3) no independent probe added ---
The gate's decision point (observeSweepDetection) is not exported from index.mjs, and
the discriminating input is verified_removable !== 0, which the replay already drives
through the real handler against the real vendored dossier. A probe would restate it.
The one importable half — the cost-report predicates — the test already imports for real
(:1117), and probes/item-06-performance-mirror.mjs covers the card arithmetic separately.

--- (4) VERDICT: item 10 VERIFIED ---
Both clauses asserted, and the negative is asserted five ways rather than once:
terminalClaims for nothing-to-remove == [], countOfType('workflow.nothing_to_remove')
=== 0, sweep.detection_observed == [], EVERY event matching /^sweep\./ == [], and no
GitHub label call.

Non-vacuity is explicit and is the part that matters here: agentTasks[DETECT] really
carries verifiedRemovable: 8 (not 0) and s3Gets contains completions/<DETECT>.json,
so the gate demonstrably READ the yield and then declined to act on it -- rather
than the code path simply never being reached.

'Full chain still dispatches' is proved by the exact unblock sequence
[SWEEP, REVIEW, QA, CI, SHIP, APPROVAL, CD] in order, one workflow.complete on the
epic with delivery 'cd' as the LAST event, storeCompletions == [WF_ID], and the run
closing on GitHub's own merge proof (mergeCommit + mergeVerifiedBy: 'github' on both
ship tickets, with a real /pulls?head= call). A separate test holds the run open at
the human Merge Approval, so 'completes' is not a bypass.

USEFUL DETAIL, honestly documented in the test at :894-897: there is no
wouldClose:false observation to look for. observeSweepDetection returns null on
verified_removable !== 0 BEFORE it publishes anything, so a productive sweep is
never observed in ANY mode. The gate is not "observing and allowing" here -- it is
short-circuiting. Sound, but it means shadow-mode telemetry on a productive sweep is
silent, so an operator cannot distinguish "gate ran and approved" from "gate never
loaded". The mode-parity test (:969) closes that by comparing full traces instead.

